[["wrb.fr",null,"[null,[\"c_fc08614222c47bfa\",\"r_af3563cad811c601\"],null,null,[[\"rc_cc6f54695c4ff3c5\",[\"Let's dive straight into how the timeouts and watchdog mechanics are configured in the `Gemini-API` codebase so you can see exactly where that **20 seconds** comes from without any guesswork.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### The Timeout Architecture in `Gemini-API`\\n\\nIn `Gemini-API` (specifically `client.py` and its connection settings), there are actually **two distinct watchdog / timeout layers** that interact during streaming:\\n\\n| Parameter / Mechanic | Where It Applies | Default Value | Role \\u0026 Behavior |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Stream Chunk / Idle Watchdog** | Inside the inner stream parsing loop (`_generate()`) | **`20` seconds** (or derived from default socket read slices) | Monitors interval between incoming byte/data deltas. Drops and attempts socket reconnection if no bytes arrive. |\\n| **Global Request Timeout** | Client-level / HTTP transport (`timeout`) | **`1\"],null,null,null,null,null,null,[1],\"en\",null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]]],[\"New York, USA\",\"SWML_DESCRIPTION_FROM_YOUR_INTERNET_ADDRESS\",false,null,\"//www.google.com/maps/vt/data\\u003dAvIzW62PGhAfUQRpZ9e4q2af_7_WOsFiVpXkQpd9LX0zB0dpJdp9NdkGa-o9tBoMCvd_Di6NgmlfyQXVg4MjqFFJU5C9KoCTOCJ6dgPFDBPpFVbqYZh0Zc64U3skCrf4jwF8niK7flGYwqgOmji5U7TBRwp7BHZh3ps424DbYR5MR0cpmx2J9OED3SQgECsR\"],null,null,\"US\",null,null,null,null,null,false,null,null,null,null,\"en\",null,null,null,true,[null,[false,false,false],[false,true,false,false,true,false],false,[[[\"Academic - Other\",3.957821E-4],[\"Coding\",0.0066171726],[\"Creative - Other\",7.6080183E-4],[\"Creative Writing\",6.888273E-4],[\"Customer Support\",7.967048E-6],[\"Daily Life Expert - Other\",8.975087E-4],[\"Daily Life Personal - Other\",8.327497E-4],[\"Data Analysis\",0.0013343863],[\"Emotio