rate())\",[[38,49,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"20 seconds (or derived from default socket read slices)\",[[0,2,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[0,10,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Monitors interval between incoming byte/data deltas. Drops and attempts socket reconnection if no bytes arrive.\"]]]]]],[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Global Request Timeout\",[[0,22,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Client-level / HTTP transport (timeout)\",[[31,38,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"120s – 450s\",[[0,4,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[7,11,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[0,11,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The ceiling for the total HTTP roundtrip / stream completion.\"]]]]]]],true]],[null,[null,0,\"Maintainers often confuse the high-level client timeout (e.g. timeout: int \\u003d 120 or 450 in client initialization) with the low-level chunk loop watchdog running inside the generator.\",[[30,55,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[62,80,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[84,87,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[123,152,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"Why You Saw 20s Without Customizing Anything\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"The 20-Second Default Idle Window:\",[[0,34,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Inside the streaming chunk generator loop, the client guards against half-open or dropped TCP connections by enforcing a per-chunk idle deadline. When no explicit override is passed, the loop checks for chunk delivery with an internal watchdog slice that defaults to 20 seconds (logging [Watchdog] Socket idle for 20s. Refreshing connection...).\",[[267,277,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[287,343,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The is_thinking Initial State Trap:\",[[4,15,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[0,35,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[