eferencing\",6.2128E-4],[\"Writing \\u0026 Rewriting - Other\",3.8133172E-4],[\"Writing From Scratch\",0.0011778112]],[[\"Output List\",4.0861126E-4],[\"Output Outline\",2.8911934E-5],[\"Output Table\",1.8358258E-5],[\"Output Citations\",2.1646309E-5],[\"Output Format\",0.001180137],[\"Change Length\",2.4561406E-4],[\"Change Ordering\",1.5318187E-4],[\"Change Structure\",3.385917E-4],[\"Adopt Persona\",2.9171418E-4],[\"Change Tone\",8.265437E-6],[\"Rhyme\",9.908769E-7],[\"Change to Specific Audience\",7.9675745E-5],[\"Change Tone / Style\",4.7403865E-4],[\"Rephrase\",1.08849774E-4],[\"Simplify / Condense\",6.442869E-5],[\"Factual / Logical Correction\",6.561896E-4],[\"Attribute-Specific Correction\",0.0013653537],[\"Pushback Circumvention\",5.8011112E-5],[\"Constraint Re-Statement\",1.9027376E-4],[\"Exact Resubmission\",3.0090884E-4],[\"Expand / Elaborate\",0.00438957],[\"Revise\",4.4427594E-4]],[[\"Positive\",0.005601703],[\"Negative\",0.004048012]]]],null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Let's dive straight into how the timeouts and watchdog mechanics are configured in the Gemini-API codebase so you can see exactly where that 20 seconds comes from without any guesswork.\",[[87,97,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[141,151,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"The Timeout Architecture in Gemini-API\",[[28,38,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"In Gemini-API (specifically client.py and its connection settings), there are actually two distinct watchdog / timeout layers that interact during streaming:\",[[3,13,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[28,37,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[87,125,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Parameter / Mechanic\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Where It Applies\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Default Value\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Role \\u0026 Behavior\"]]]]]],[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Stream Chunk / Idle Watchdog\",[[0,28,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Inside the inner stream parsing loop (_generate())\",[[38,49,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"20 seconds (or derived from default socket read slices)\",[[0,2,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[0,10,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Monitors interval between incoming byte/data deltas. Drops and attempts socket reconnection if no bytes arrive.\"]]]]]],[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Global Request Timeout\",[[0,22,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Client-level / HTTP transport (timeout)\",[[31,38,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"120s – 450s\",[[0,4,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[7,11,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[0,11,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The ceiling for the total HTTP roundtrip / stream completion.\"]]]]]]],true]],[null,[null,0,\"Maintainers often confuse the high-level client timeout (e.g. timeout: int \\u003d 120 or 450 in client initialization) with the low-level chunk loop watchdog running inside the generator.\",[[30,55,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[62,80,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[84,87,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[123,152,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"Why You Saw 20s Without Customizing Anything\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"The 20-Second Default Idle Window:\",[[0,34,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Inside the streaming chunk generator loop, the client guards against half-open or dropped TCP connections by enforcing a per-chunk idle deadline. When no explicit override is passed, the loop checks for chunk delivery with an internal watchdog slice that defaults to 20 seconds (logging [Watchdog] Socket idle for 20s. Refreshing connection...).\",[[267,277,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[287,343,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The is_thinking Initial State Trap:\",[[4,15,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[0,35,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"In client.py (around line 1570), is_thinking is initialized unconditionally to False:\",[[3,12,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[33,44,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[79,84,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,null,null,[\"is_thinking \\u003d False\\n\",\"python\"]],[null,[null,0,\"The stall threshold logic evaluates:\"]],[null,null,null,[\"stall_threshold \\u003d self.timeout if is_thinking else min(self.timeout, self.watchdog_timeout)\\n\",\"python\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Since is_thinking starts as False, the threshold immediately collapses to min(self.timeout, 20) \\u003d 20 seconds.\",[[6,17,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[28,33,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[74,95,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[98,108,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"During extended reasoning (especially on complex chain-of-thought prompts), the server can easily take 25\"]]]]]]]]]],1]]]]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",true,[[[[1004,\"Longer\",5,null,[\"expand\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/expand/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1005,\"Shorter\",6,null,[\"compress\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/compress/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1002,\"Don't personalize\",2,null,[\"person_cancel\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/person_cancel/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1001,\"Try again\",1,null,[\"refresh\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/refresh/default/24px.svg\",null,true]]]]],null,2,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,1,1]"]]
